1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:04,140
Why did Shiva burn his own devotees' three cities to ashes with one arrow?

2
00:00:05,170 --> 00:00:10,900
The Shiva Purana tells that Tarakasura's three sons asked as a boon: cities of gold,

3
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,060
silver, and iron,

4
00:00:12,170 --> 00:00:15,130
three flying cities. Denied immortality,

5
00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:20,406
They chose their own death: once in a thousand years,

6
00:00:20,406 --> 00:00:21,807
when all three align,

7
00:00:21,807 --> 00:00:24,009
a single arrow could pierce them.

8
00:00:24,009 --> 00:00:25,010
Across Tripura,

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:27,550
[Tarakaksha] Shiva was worshipped.

10
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:31,080
'Only Mahadev can shoot such an arrow,' '...and why would Mahadev...'

11
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:37,008
'...ever burn his devotees?' But from the three brothers' might,

12
00:00:37,008 --> 00:00:38,270
heaven began to burn.

13
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:41,486
The defeated devas sought refuge with Mahadev,

14
00:00:41,486 --> 00:00:43,460
so to the devas, Mahadev said:

15
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:45,300
[Shiva] They are my devotees,

16
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:48,220
[Shiva] as long as their devotion lasts,

17
00:00:49,380 --> 00:00:50,480
[Shiva] I will not slay them.

18
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:53,080
Then Lord Vishnu cast an illusion,

19
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:56,028
And Tripura's people forgot to worship Shiva.

20
00:00:56,028 --> 00:00:57,907
Mahadev's chariot was readied,

21
00:00:57,907 --> 00:00:59,410
sun and moon its wheels,

22
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:01,191
Brahma drove the chariot,

23
00:01:01,191 --> 00:01:03,052
and Vishnu became the arrow.

24
00:01:03,052 --> 00:01:04,580
A thousand years later,

25
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:06,222
all three cities aligned.

26
00:01:06,222 --> 00:01:07,270
A single arrow...

27
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:15,850
...and Tripura turned to ashes.

28
00:01:17,430 --> 00:01:18,628
Even while burning,

29
00:01:18,628 --> 00:01:20,710
Tarakaksha called out to Mahadev:

30
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:23,660
[Tarakaksha] May my heart remain devoted to you in every birth.

31
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:27,537
It wasn't the flying cities protecting Tripura,

32
00:01:27,537 --> 00:01:30,139
it was devotion. Once devotion was lost,

33
00:01:30,139 --> 00:01:31,830
a single arrow was enough.

